WEBVTT

NOTE
Automatic English captions. Generated locally and checked with additional audio decodes; not fully audited by listening.

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.940
Building a workflow usually starts with a
blank canvas, but sometimes the idea is

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.920
clearer in your head than on the screen.
Chat gives you a different starting point.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.660
You describe the system you want in plain
language, and Sim can turn that into

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:21.460
blocks, test the result, fix what breaks,
and keep refining it with you. It's a more

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.160
conversational way to get from idea to
working automation. Let me show you how it

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.720
works. You can build a whole workflow
without dragging a single block. You just

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.840
open a chat and describe what you want.
Say you want an agent that turns an idea

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.360
into a finished post, a written draft, a
hero image, a slide deck, and a voiceover.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:46.580
You ask for it, and the whole thing builds
itself, every block wired up. Before you

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.200
even ask, it runs the whole thing itself
just to see if it holds together.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.900
The image step fails. It was missing an
aspect ratio. It catches that on its own,

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.640
fixes it, and runs again. Clean.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.780
Then it shows you what it made. Every step
that ran. The draft, the image, the deck,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.580
the audio, so you can check it before you
trust it.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.260
You hand it a real idea, and it drafts a
few versions at once, scores each one, and

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.260
keeps the best.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.260
One more message, and it's deployed. A
live endpoint ready for whatever you send

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.260
it.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.220
You went from a blank canvas to a working
system without leaving the conversation.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.220
Open a new chat and see what you can
build.
